<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Build a static site and publish it to a remote nginx container by scp (push model).

.DESCRIPTION
    Copy to `publish.ps1` in your app repo and adapt the CONFIG block below. This is the PUSH
    publish model: build locally, then scp the output to the box's bind-mount directory. Use it
    when the box cannot (or should not) hold a clone of the repo -- a private repo, or a box with
    no repo access. If the box CAN clone the repo directly, prefer the pull model instead
    (publish/deploy-pull.sh + the systemd timer units) -- see README.md's "Push or pull?".

    No restart needed on the box: nginx reads files per request off the read-only mount. (A
    `docker compose restart` is only needed when nginx.conf itself changes, which this never
    ships.) If your build hashes asset filenames (Vite etc.), a fresh index.html always references
    the assets that shipped alongside it, so there's no stale-asset window.

    Publishes via a remote STAGING directory, not a direct scp into the live web-root dir:

      1. scp the build into a throwaway "<dir>.new" next to the live dir. The network transfer --
         the slow, failure-prone step -- happens here, and the live dir is untouched while it runs.
      2. Only once that fully succeeds, swap it in with a single ssh call doing a local (same-host,
         no-network) delete-then-copy -- so the window where the live dir is momentarily empty is
         milliseconds, not however long an scp over the network takes.

    Why this shape (all proven the hard way on the reference implementation, roshne/Tooling's
    tools-site):
      * A network blip or interrupted scp leaves the live site exactly as it was -- it never
        empties the live dir with nothing to replace it.
      * The live dir's own directory ENTRY is kept, never removed-and-recreated -- the container's
        bind mount is a live reference to that directory; replacing the directory itself (vs. its
        contents) risks orphaning the mount.
      * scp's source is "<dir>/." (trailing dot), not "<dir>/": `scp -r <dir> host:existing-dir/`
        NESTS (creates a "<dir>" folder inside the target) whenever the target already exists,
        which the staging dir always does. The trailing-dot form copies the CONTENTS instead.
      * Explicit $LASTEXITCODE checks after each native call: PowerShell only auto-throws on a
        native nonzero exit under 7.4+ with $PSNativeCommandUseErrorActionPreference on. The
        checks make failure loud on any pwsh.
      * Uses only ordinary coreutils on the box (find, cp -a, rm -rf) -- no rsync (not always
        installed).

.PARAMETER Server
    SSH target for the box (user@host).

.PARAMETER RemoteDir
    The app's stack directory on the box (holds compose.yaml + nginx.conf, shipped once at setup,
    plus the web-root dir this script reships every run).

.EXAMPLE
    .\publish.ps1
#>
[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [string] $Server = '<user>@<host>',
    [string] $RemoteDir = '/opt/stacks/<app>'
)

Set-StrictMode -Version Latest
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'

# === CONFIG: adapt these two to your app ===
$LocalDirName = 'dist'    # the build output dir under this repo (e.g. dist, build; or 'site' if there's no build)
$RemoteDirName = 'dist'   # the web-root dir name under $RemoteDir on the box
# ===========================================

$localPath = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot $LocalDirName

# === BUILD: adapt (or delete) this block ===
# The reference implementation (tools-site) runs `npm run build --prefix $PSScriptRoot`, which
# runs the build with its cwd set to this repo regardless of where you invoke the script from.
# Replace the command to match your build; DELETE the whole block if the site is prebuilt or has
# no build step (e.g. a hand-authored one-pager). Keep the $LASTEXITCODE check so a failed build
# never publishes a stale/empty output.
Write-Output "Building (npm run build)..."
& npm run build --prefix $PSScriptRoot
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    throw "build failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE)"
}
# ===========================================

$localIndex = Join-Path $localPath 'index.html'
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $localIndex -PathType Leaf)) {
    throw "No $LocalDirName/index.html at $localIndex -- refusing to publish an empty/incomplete build"
}

$remoteLive    = "$RemoteDir/$RemoteDirName"
$remoteStaging = "$RemoteDir/$RemoteDirName.new"

Write-Output "Staging at $Server`:$remoteStaging..."
& ssh $Server "rm -rf '$remoteStaging' && mkdir -p '$remoteStaging'"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    throw "ssh staging setup at '$remoteStaging' on $Server failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE)"
}

$stagingTarget = "${Server}:${remoteStaging}/"
Write-Output "Copying $localPath -> $stagingTarget"
& scp -r (Join-Path $localPath '.') $stagingTarget
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    throw "scp to $stagingTarget failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE) -- the live site at '$remoteLive' was not touched"
}

Write-Output "Swapping the staged build into $Server`:$remoteLive (local copy on the box, no network)..."
& ssh $Server "mkdir -p '$remoteLive' && find '$remoteLive' -mindepth 1 -delete && cp -a '$remoteStaging'/. '$remoteLive'/ && rm -rf '$remoteStaging'"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    throw "swap into '$remoteLive' on $Server failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE) -- live site may be inconsistent; re-run this script"
}

Write-Output "Published. Content-only changes are live immediately -- no restart needed."
Write-Output "(A restart is only required when nginx.conf changes, which this script never ships.)"
